  "body": "C-library inputs/results and unload, OpenCL setup/failure cleanup, TLS listeners/cache/wire/connect paths and scoped File owners retain or release their resources across normal return, error, trap and cancellation. Compiler workers and preserved frames keep original typed owners alive; writes and I/O errors agree with the interpreter.\n\nRaw pointer offsets use defined unsigned pointer-width arithmetic. Raw buffers still require manual freeing; string conversions copy borrowed input and return counted managed leaves. New tests cover boundary addresses without dereference, old signed-overflow rejection, independent buffer lifetimes and last-owner reclamation.\n\nThis bundles roadmap items54\u201373 on the accepted PR122 squash. All42 original implementation/documentation commits and original regression/negative controls remain, plus the pointer and raw-memory repairs. Accepted diagnostics are inherited exactly. Fake OpenCL APIs verify lifetime paths, not GPU hardware execution; F16/128-bit and WebAssembly pointer width remain separate acceptance.\n\nGuarded checks pass: eight native pointer/raw-memory/resource-frame tests,65 library units, focused clippy and formatting, zero ignored. Smaller-candidate library input/result/resource controls and independent Linux/ARM/Intel pointer sanitizer evidence also pass. The equivalent-tree final rebase preserves tested native bytes and hashes. Full Linux, bench, regular ARM/Intel macOS, ARM/Intel GC stress and roadmap_docs must pass at the final head before squash; independent evidence does not replace these gates. Phases2\u20136 retain explicit remaining acceptance in PLAN.\n",
